WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.960
Cut out one boom, with a short length d z, and the skin on either side.

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:11.431
Along the boom, the bending stress changes from sigma to sigma plus d sigma.

00:00:11.431 --> 00:00:15.193
The skin pushes on it with shear flows q one and q two.

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:23.207
Force balance along the boom gives q two minus q one equals minus d sigma by d z, times B r.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:34.178
With only a vertical load and I x y zero, d sigma by d z is S y over I x x, times y.

00:00:34.178 --> 00:00:40.600
So the jump is minus S y over I x x, times B r y r.

00:00:41.566 --> 00:00:46.654
Between booms the skin carries no direct stress, so the shear flow is constant.

00:00:46.654 --> 00:00:49.166
It only changes when it crosses a boom.

00:00:49.566 --> 00:00:59.382
For this channel, I x x is four times three hundred times two hundred squared: forty eight million.

00:00:59.382 --> 00:01:03.646
So S y over I x x is ten to the minus four.

00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:07.749
Start at the free edge, where q is zero.

00:01:07.749 --> 00:01:14.685
Crossing boom one: zero minus ten to the minus four, times three hundred, times two hundred.

00:01:14.685 --> 00:01:17.173
Minus six newtons per millimeter.

00:01:17.566 --> 00:01:18.133
Your turn.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:21.366
Pause here and do checkpoint two point one in your guide.

00:01:24.599 --> 00:01:28.738
Boom two adds another minus six: minus twelve in the web.

00:01:28.738 --> 00:01:34.329
Boom three sits at minus two hundred, so it adds plus six: back to minus six.

00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:38.759
And boom four brings it to zero at the free edge, as it must.

00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:47.019
In a closed section there is no free edge to start from.

00:01:47.019 --> 00:01:49.325
So we make one: cut any wall.

00:01:50.332 --> 00:01:53.120
With the cut, it's an open section.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.944
March around from the cut, jumping at each boom.

00:01:56.944 --> 00:01:59.572
That's the basic shear flow, q b.

00:02:00.032 --> 00:02:06.752
Closing the cut adds one constant shear flow, q s zero, all the way around the cell.

00:02:07.132 --> 00:02:09.604
To find q s zero, use moments.

00:02:09.604 --> 00:02:17.761
If the load passes through the shear center, there's another condition: the section must not twist.

00:02:17.761 --> 00:02:22.292
The integral of q d s over G t around the cell is zero.
